+### Guild Hall filter chips get the same background-bleed fix as patch 0315's rows (patch 0316)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Bug Fix
+
+- Fixed the Guild Hall filter chips (All/Combat/Economy/Roster/Care/Unlocks) bleeding the background art through, same as the row fix last patch
+```
+
+Same bug patch 0315 fixed on `.guild-upgrade-row`/`.guild-built-row`,
+spotted on the one row of controls that patch missed: the inactive
+filter chips were still `background: transparent`, so the Guild Hall
+art behind the tab showed straight through them too. Now carries the
+same `color-mix(in srgb, var(--panel) 88%, transparent)` wash as
+everything else on this tab. Hover on an inactive chip swaps to solid
+`var(--panel-2)` now (was `transparent` before, which combined with the
+border-only hover feedback read as barely-there) -- matches the row
+hover treatment right below it. The active chip's solid brass fill was
+never part of this bug and is unchanged.
+
+**Verified:** pulled `app.css` fresh from `main` (patch 0315 was
+already live) before editing. `npx tsc --noEmit` and a full `vite
+build` passing clean against a fresh clone -- CSS-only change, no
+`.tsx` touched this patch.
